 @lapz6758  Some people seem to have gotten 1000-1200 watt power supplies with 12 pin connectors straight out of the PSU itself, that splits in half to two 8 pins...

I dunno if those output 500w or 600w that is halved, but a 8 pin is suppose to handle 150 watts to a GPU, those PSU are going to fry your GPU if they output more than 300w for each 12 pin split to dual 8 pints...

I wonder if Nvidia knew this is gonna happen once the 12 pin connectors starts becoming common and PSU manufacturers decided "hey why not just use 12 pin slots on the PSU instead of regular 8 pin slots, and use dividers?"

